# The two things `npm run discord:plan` needs, as the shape of the file it reads.
#
#     cp discord.env.example discord.env
#
# `discord.env` is ignored by git, and `tools/discord.ts` refuses to run at all if
# it has ever been *tracked* — a bot token in git is a bot token in every clone
# and every fork, and unlike a leaked keystore there is no recovering from it but
# to reset the token. Never paste either value into a chat; put them here.
#
# DISCORD_TOKEN
#   Developer Portal → your application → Bot → Reset Token. It is a password: it
#   acts as the bot, which can post as itself and read every channel it can see.
#
# DISCORD_GUILD
#   The server's id, from Discord with Developer Mode on: right-click the server →
#   Copy Server ID. It can be left empty while the bot is in exactly one server —
#   the tool uses that one — and filling it in is what stops a run configuring the
#   wrong community once the bot is in more than one.
DISCORD_TOKEN=
DISCORD_GUILD=
